# Granular landslide simulations

This sandbox contains Basilisk simulations developed during my M1 internship at Institut Jean Le Rond d'Alembert with Pierre-Yves Lagrée.

The objective is to model dry granular landslides using depth-averaged approaches and to compare the results with other numerical models and experimental data.

## 1D simulations

* [Dry granular collapse – comparison with HySEA](dry_landslide_comparison_hysea.c)
  Saint-Venant simulation of the dry granular collapse experiment of Poulain et al. (2023), using the Pouliquen–Forterre basal friction law. Results are compared with experimental data and the non-hydrostatic HySEA model.

* [Dry granular collapse – comparison with SHALTOP](dry_landslide_comparison_shaltop.c)
  Basilisk implementation of a SHALTOP-type formulation for the same granular collapse configuration, including topographic and curvature corrections. Results are compared with reference SHALTOP profiles.

## 2D simulations

* **2D granular landslide – in preparation**
  Extension of the granular landslide simulations to two dimensions.

## Context

These simulations were developed as part of a study on numerical modelling of granular landslides and their possible application to landslide-generated waves.

